00:37:22,812 --> 00:37:23,812
Ms. Kuroki.

531
00:37:27,854 --> 00:37:29,562
Wait, Ms. Kuroki.

532
00:37:33,229 --> 00:37:34,437
Where is Mr. Muranishi?

533
00:37:34,521 --> 00:37:37,021
Actually, I'm not really sure.

534
00:37:37,104 --> 00:37:39,646
Okay, get on set. Let's get started.

535
00:37:39,729 --> 00:37:40,979
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

536
00:37:41,062 --> 00:37:43,396
-Hey. Sugihara, lie down stage right.
-Sure.

537
00:37:43,479 --> 00:37:45,312
Yoshida, lie down stage left.

538
00:37:48,812 --> 00:37:49,812
Good.

539
00:37:53,937 --> 00:37:55,896
Yoshida, a little more this way.

540
00:37:55,979 --> 00:37:57,646
That's good there.

541
00:38:02,021 --> 00:38:03,729
-Rugby, pull this one back.
-Yes, sir.

542
00:38:03,812 --> 00:38:06,229
You're not going to be in this,
Mr. Muranishi?

543
00:38:06,896 --> 00:38:09,479
What's wrong?
Is there a problem with that?

544
00:38:10,062 --> 00:38:13,521
I can't stand this script.
Is this really what you want to film?

545
00:38:14,021 --> 00:38:16,771
It's not whether I want to do it.
It's what people want.

546
00:38:16,854 --> 00:38:19,479
I thought that making it together
was what it's all about.

547
00:38:19,562 --> 00:38:22,146
That's just your assumption.
I need to give people what they want.

548
00:38:22,229 --> 00:38:25,229
-I want to make this with you!
-Don't be so selfish!

549
00:38:25,979 --> 00:38:27,229
You're a pro, aren't you?

550
00:38:27,812 --> 00:38:29,812
This entire company relies on us.

551
00:38:29,896 --> 00:38:32,396
We need to give
everyone here a livelihood!

552
00:38:32,479 --> 00:38:34,104
Satellite TV is how we'll survive.

553
00:38:34,187 --> 00:38:36,271
We have to do
whatever it takes to succeed!

554
00:38:36,354 --> 00:38:37,604
To do that, we need to fulfill--

555
00:38:37,687 --> 00:38:40,187
You want to change your style
for such a lame reason?

556
00:38:40,271 --> 00:38:42,479
You want to make this garbage
for that purpose?

557
00:38:42,562 --> 00:38:44,687
This will never surpass
I Like It S&amp;M Style!

558
00:38:44,771 --> 00:38:46,479
Nothing ever will!

559
00:38:47,604 --> 00:38:50,271
Don't be stupid!
Why does everyone think that?

560
00:38:51,021 --> 00:38:52,396
That was made by pure chance

561
00:38:52,479 --> 00:38:57,021
thanks to the convergence
of miracle upon miracle!

562
00:38:57,104 --> 00:38:59,229
You can't plan something like that!

563
00:39:02,479 --> 00:39:04,479
Let's do this! Let's roll!

564
00:39:04,562 --> 00:39:05,604
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

565
00:39:09,062 --> 00:39:10,146
Mr. Muranishi.

566
00:39:13,479 --> 00:39:17,021
Please take back what you just said.

567
00:39:19,937 --> 00:39:22,021
Everyone will do their best filming this.

568
00:39:22,521 --> 00:39:23,896
I expect the same from you.

569
00:39:27,812 --> 00:39:28,937
Let's go.

570
00:39:29,687 --> 00:39:30,604
Yes, sir.

571
00:39:32,312 --> 00:39:33,146
Kuroki…

572
00:39:33,229 --> 00:39:34,062
Junko!

573
00:39:38,771 --> 00:39:41,229
It turned out just like you wanted.

574
00:39:43,812 --> 00:39:44,646
What?

575
00:40:07,812 --> 00:40:10,146
Mr. Muranishi,
let's call it quits for today.

576
00:40:10,229 --> 00:40:11,354
No. We're filming.

577
00:40:48,312 --> 00:40:52,146
Would it be all right
if I took the place of Ms. Kuroki?

578
00:44:09,646 --> 00:44:14,646
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey

